# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 13 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Example 19.1 (z parameters)]

r1,1,2,20
r2,2,0,40
r3,2,3,30

analysis: dc
tool: port
n1: 1
n2: 3
kind: z
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[AS7's Example 19.2 (a two-port as an element)]

e,1,0,100
z,1,2
r,2,0,10

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: The four parameters are pinned in Expert Mode, which works here because this is a plain solve rather than an equivalent.
equations: z11 = 40
equations: z12 = 20j
equations: z21 = 30j
equations: z22 = 50
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


